# Wonder UI Component & Styling Patterns

## File structure

Each component lives in `src/components/ComponentName/`:

- `ComponentName.tsx` — component + exported props types
- `ComponentName.module.css` — scoped styles
- `index.ts` — barrel re-export of component and types

Register new components in `src/index.ts`.

## React conventions

- Named function exports: `export function Button(...)`.
- Export props as `ComponentNameProps`; export variant unions separately when reused (`CardVariant`, `AlertVariant`).
- Extend native HTML attributes when wrapping a DOM element:

```tsx
export type ButtonProps = {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary';
} & React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>;
```

- Set defaults in destructuring (`variant = 'primary'`).
- Always accept and merge `className` via the local `cx` helper (defined per file, not shared).
- Spread `...props` onto the underlying native element last.
- Use `useId()` for form controls; wire `label`/`htmlFor`, `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`, and `role="alert"` for errors.

## Class composition

```tsx
function cx(...classes: (string | undefined | false)[]) {
  return classes.filter(Boolean).join(' ');
}

className={cx(styles.base, styles[variant], condition && styles.modifier, className)}
```

Map variant/size props directly to CSS module class names (`styles[variant]`, `styles[size]`).

## CSS modules & design tokens

- Import styles: `import styles from './ComponentName.module.css'`.
- Use `--wonder-*` tokens from `src/styles/tokens.css` — never hardcode colors, spacing, radii, or motion values.
- Base class for layout, separate classes for variants/sizes/states.
- CamelCase class names in CSS modules (`.inputError`, `.wrapperDisabled`).

### Token categories

| Category | Examples |
|----------|----------|
| Color | `--wonder-color-primary`, `--wonder-color-text-muted`, `--wonder-color-surface` |
| Spacing | `--wonder-space-1` … `--wonder-space-6` |
| Typography | `--wonder-font-size-*`, `--wonder-font-weight-*`, `--wonder-font-family` |
| Shape | `--wonder-radius-sm` … `--wonder-radius-full` |
| Shadow | `--wonder-shadow-soft`, `--wonder-shadow-inset`, `--wonder-shadow-3d-*` |
| Motion | `--wonder-transition-fast`, `--wonder-transition-press` |
| A11y | `--wonder-tap-target` (48px min interactive height) |

### Interactive 3D press (buttons, toggles)

Follow the pattern in `src/styles/depth.css`:

- Rest: bottom depth via `box-shadow` (no blur)
- Hover: `translateY(-1px)`, deepen shadow
- Active: `translateY(var(--wonder-depth-md))`, collapse shadow
- Disabled: `opacity: 0.55`, `cursor: not-allowed`, flatten depth

Ghost/non-3D variants skip the shadow press; use `scale(0.98)` on active instead.

### Common style rules

- Border radius: `--wonder-radius-lg` for inputs, `--wonder-radius-xl` for cards, `--wonder-radius-full` for pills/buttons.
- Focus rings: `outline: none` + colored `box-shadow` ring using token color at ~20% opacity.
- Disabled inputs: `opacity: 0.55`, muted background.
- Card tints use `--wonder-color-sky`, `--wonder-color-butter`, `--wonder-color-blush`, `--wonder-color-mint`.

## Accessibility checklist

- Decorative icons/spinners: `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Loading spinner: `role="status"` + `aria-label`.
- Alerts: `role="alert"`; dismiss button needs `aria-label`.
- Form errors: `role="alert"` on error text, `aria-invalid` on input.
